    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2379" root="برك" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَبْرَكٌ</span></b>  <i>A place where camels lie upon their
breasts:</i> pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَبَارِكٌ</span>. (Msb.) You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُلَانٌ لَيْسَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَهُ مِبْرَكٌ جَمَلٍ</span> [<i>Such a one has not a place in which
a camel lies;</i> meaning <i>he does not possess a single
camel</i>]. (S.)

